  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nIs the lease of a residential unit at ₱15,000 per month subject to VAT?\n\n### Short Answer\nNo, the lease of a residential unit at ₱15,000 per month is not subject to VAT.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practical terms, if a residential unit is leased for ₱15,000 per month, the lessor is not required to charge VAT on the rental payments. This exemption is beneficial for both landlords and tenants, as it reduces the overall cost of leasing residential properties. Landlords should ensure that their rental agreements reflect this exemption to avoid any potential tax liabilities.",
